    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with three clear pillars in our offense. **Trevor Story** leads the charge with a 73.92 efficiency score, bolstered significantly by a favorable matchup against Nick Martinez and a wind-out forecast that provides a massive ceiling for extra-base hits. Following closely are **Corbin Carroll** (68.74) and **James Wood** (68.43). **James Wood** is particularly well-positioned as the leadoff hitter against Sandy Alcantara; his combination of premium spot in the order (+10%) and the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which creates an elite environment for his stolen base upside\u2014makes him an essential engine for our category balance. **Tyler Soderstrom** (63.88) rounds out our strongest quartet, leveraging an elite park factor that adds 16% to his base projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the sheet was keeping **Travis Bazzana** (44.91) on the bench. Despite a solid xwOBA of .382, he ultimately fell short of the starting threshold due to a lower overall efficiency projection compared to **Seiya Suzuki** and **Jose Caballero**, both of whom are pushed into the lineup despite tougher matchups against deGrom and Henderson, respectively, due to their higher raw output metrics. Owners should exercise caution with **Jose Caballero** and **Seiya Suzuki** today; both face daunting opposing starters, and their projected scores are tethered to the high volatility of facing elite arms. Furthermore, while **Corbin Carroll** remains a top play, he faces a significant risk factor today\u2014a highly efficient catcher with a 1.87s pop time\u2014which necessitates a slight downward adjustment to his stolen base success probability.",
